From fca583181d7143f82b869abe952d0e295c124a77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code Review <claude-review@example.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:40:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add shared rate limiting (Upstash) and error monitoring
 (Sentry)

Rate limiting:
- rateLimit.js now uses Upstash Redis when UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL and
  UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN are set, so limits hold across Vercel's
  serverless instances (the old in-memory limiter only counted within
  one process). Falls back to the in-memory limiter automatically
  when Upstash isn't configured, so local dev needs no account.
- API changed from rateLimit(key, opts) to createLimiter(name, opts)
  returning an async .check(key); limiters are created once at module
  scope. register, forgot-password, and qr/create updated.

Error monitoring:
- add @sentry/nextjs (pinned 11.5.0); sentry.client.config.js and
  sentry.server.config.js initialize only when a DSN is set, so
  builds and local dev work before Sentry exists
- next.config.js wrapped with withSentryConfig (merged with the
  existing /r/:slug rewrite). Verified the build succeeds with no
  SENTRY_* vars and with only a DSN; org/project/authToken are only
  needed for source-map upload (readable stack traces)
- _error.js captures page-render errors
- explicit Sentry.captureException added where errors were previously
  caught and only logged (redirect route, password-reset email send,
  scan logging at warning level), since those never reach the
  automatic unhandled-error capture

.env.example documents the new variables.
